{"stats":{"took":74,"total":7,"estimate":false,"maxScore":171.08499},"results":[{"_meta":{"score":171.08499},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20150021842,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"8760b890641449b5993dac88f0fab51f","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Man/System Technology And Life Support"],"keywords":["biomedical","astroskin","psychophysiology"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20150021842,"ear":"NO","id":"ebcbd25a977d47d194c248b5e7979eb9","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["ARC-E-DAA-TN26234","Report Number: ARC-E-DAA-TN26234"],"fundingNumbers":[{"number":"NNX12AB08A","submissionId":20150021842,"id":"2fa10e5ff9c548beb56eb65275f919a4","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"},{"number":"WBS 516724.02.01.21.02.04","submissionId":20150021842,"id":"b9d5c340cbe14cf5abf1bff77202734d","type":"WBS"}],"title":"Evaluation of the Accuracy of Astroskin as a Behavioral Health Self-Monitoring System for Spaceflight","stiType":"PRESENTATION","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2015-11-25T12:43:09.6570000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20150021842,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Kumar, Arun"},"organization":{"name":"San Jose State Univ.","location":"CA, United States"}},"id":"264ea7d9463141f39830729b5ccde0f8"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20150021842,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Levin, Edwin"},"organization":{"name":"Hartnell Coll","location":"Salinas, CA, United States"}},"id":"347b6ea7a67f4107bf3b3a926664271d"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":20150021842,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Cowings, Patricia"},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"47001a6a6a7f47a8a26478accb4722cb"},{"sequence":3,"submissionId":20150021842,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Toscano, William B."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"73da9b9c577e410192c1dedf3095fed2"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Presentation","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20150021842,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2015-11-25T12:43:09.6570000+00:00","center":{"code":"ARC","name":"Ames Research Center","id":"4540cd94d24c4bf29f8773a27faf96b2"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"In space, there is a need to monitor astronauts' vital signs and assess their readiness to perform specific tasks during a mission. Currently, NASA does not have the capability to noninvasively monitor crew for extended periods of time. The Canadian Space Agency is working with the Psychophysiology Lab at NASA ARC to determine if the Astroskin could be used as a solution to this problem. Astroskin, a commercially available garment with built-in biosensors, can be comfortably worn under clothing or a spacesuit and relay information to the crewman's own mobile device. Data can also be sent wirelessly to the on-board Exploration Medical System. To determine if Astroskin meets requirements for health monitoring, it must first be validated in spaceflight analog environments. In the current study Astroskin data will be compared to traditional biomedical instrument measures of electrocardiography (ECG), respiration rate, and systolic blood pressure. The data will be recorded during Autogenic Feedback Training Exercise (AFTE), which is a type of physiological self-regulation training designed for astronauts. The data will also be recorded during simulations of the Orion spacecraft re-entry. The results to date suggest that Astroskin is a suitable ambulatory monitoring system that allows astronauts to self-diagnose and self-regulate adverse autonomic nervous system responses to sustained exposure to microgravity of spaceflight.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","meetings":[{"country":"United States","submissionId":20150021842,"sponsors":[{"organizationId":"99c48022232a45a1ab82c3ac682ca3c1","meta":{"organization":{"name":"Hartnell Coll","location":"Salinas, CA, United States"}},"meetingId":"b6743520cab94422bb463c40b1ee3ff3","id":"4a19ad06d49543859db081d28f3f4a40"}],"name":"Annual Summer STEM Internship Symposium","location":"Salinas, CA","id":"b6743520cab94422bb463c40b1ee3ff3","startDate":"2015-08-22T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20150021842,"id":"1ee55315edf644aebcf87b063965f006","publicationDate":"2015-08-22T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20150021842.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20150021842/downloads/20150021842.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20150021842/downloads/20150021842.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20150021842/downloads/20150021842.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":118.61612},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20180008707,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"821cbc1080cc4436a307e32a5cf4f8e8","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Man/System Technology And Life Support"],"keywords":["Vital signs","Astroskin","Biosensors"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","eccnNumber":"","submissionId":20180008707,"ear":"NO","id":"9c034fdb1aa6473d8f9b4399c1d48117","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["ARC-E-DAA-TN38215","Report Number: ARC-E-DAA-TN38215"],"fundingNumbers":[{"number":"NNA14AA60C","submissionId":20180008707,"id":"d2b1026e9f5646e695b5b629f0de03f2","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"},{"number":"NNA14AB82C","submissionId":20180008707,"id":"99d6ad92d1094fd98920a11b75aea8ab","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"},{"number":"NNA13AC87C","submissionId":20180008707,"id":"c9902d563a8c43a5b548a776728c54db","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"},{"number":"NNA16BD14C","submissionId":20180008707,"id":"5049cf375f8d49258a0da7c2adc480bd","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"}],"title":"Biosensor Integration Development ExMC/Canadian Space Agency Collaboration","stiType":"PRESENTATION","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2018-12-20T13:21:15.5600000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20180008707,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Krihak, M."},"organization":{"name":"Universities Space Research Association (USRA)","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"0467b332d24549a38fe959122b3460c7"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20180008707,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Wolfe, S."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"badd153b70fd48aaaab79dca506c4a62"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":20180008707,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Lindsey, A."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"978db409b5b64c479aa0ddf5e0397139"},{"sequence":3,"submissionId":20180008707,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Middour, C."},"organization":{"name":"Millennium Engineering and Integration Co.","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"eb2f886d83294cbd8d98161fb5c905ba"},{"sequence":4,"submissionId":20180008707,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Toscano, W."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"7b2411516385466cabd67d13fc588e77"},{"sequence":5,"submissionId":20180008707,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Winther, S."},"organization":{"name":"Wyle Labs., Inc.","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"7aa566f04c2b45ebaf4eeb5cc4d6a88b"},{"sequence":6,"submissionId":20180008707,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Marker, N."},"organization":{"name":"SGT, Inc.","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"f016fa82a8c9430d95bc24d3cdb841b5"},{"sequence":7,"submissionId":20180008707,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Shaw, T."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"15b74da3d38f4287bf4ae3bf6b9825ca"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Presentation","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20180008707,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2018-12-20T13:21:15.5600000+00:00","center":{"code":"ARC","name":"Ames Research Center","id":"4540cd94d24c4bf29f8773a27faf96b2"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"In support of the NASA Human Research Program Exploration Medical Capability (ExMC) Element, NASA Ames Research Center (ARC) established a collaborative effort with the Canadian Space Agency (CSA). The collaboration focuses on leveraging CSA capability in the areas of biosensors and decision support that will augment future development of such components for Exploration Missions. The CSA advancement of biosensors enables NASA to focus on the integration and data management associated with these types of components through the system currently under development by the Medical Data Architecture (MDA) project. This approach has enabled the establishment of a successful collaborative working relationship between ExMC and CSA.Applying lessons learned from the fiscal year 2016 (FY16) Human Exploration Research Analog (HERA) campaign, CSA and NASA ARC developed a solution to provide real-time feedback to researchers who monitor the collection of vital signs data from a wearable Astroskin garment. The advances in the interfaces included the development of an iPad application (by CSA) to wirelessly forward the vital signs data to the MDA system, which collected the vital signs data through a receiver developed by NASA ARC. The development of these interfaces aims to provide communications between the Astroskin and the MDA system such that data may be seamlessly collected, stored and retrieved by the MDA. The first steps towards this goal were demonstrated in FY16. In FY17, ExMC will complete the first in a series of test beds that establishes a system to automate collection and management of vital sign data from the Astroskin, and other sources of data, to provide information for a crewmember to make medical decisions. In addition, the MDA Test Bed 1 will enable CSA to evaluate and optimize biosensor advancement and facilitate decision support algorithm development.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","meetings":[{"submissionId":20180008707,"name":"NASA Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, TX, United States","id":"21a33287a5924b6f822947a5abe936f5"},{"country":"United States","submissionId":20180008707,"endDate":"2017-01-27T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"meta":{"organization":{"name":"NASA Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, TX, United States"}},"meetingId":"82f36c1b77ee49519a7b76faf23b8b4a","id":"34da1e9036df4d40aca92e41b0f55b2c"}],"name":"2017 Human Research Program Investigators'' Workshop","location":"Galveston, TX","id":"82f36c1b77ee49519a7b76faf23b8b4a","startDate":"2017-01-23T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20180008707,"id":"5c25867bd7e440d09b3a33068b0bbdf9","publicationDate":"2017-01-25T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[{"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","id":20190000277,"type":"SEE_ALSO","title":"Biosensor Integration Development ExMC/Canadian Space Agency Collaboration","stiType":"ABSTRACT","distribution":"PUBLIC","status":"CURATED"}],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20180008707.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20180008707/downloads/20180008707.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20180008707/downloads/20180008707.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20180008707/downloads/20180008707.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":113.02463},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20190000277,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"016498c9e9a845969b254f8f08425973","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Man/System Technology And Life Support"],"keywords":["Astroskin","Vital signs","Biosensors"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","eccnNumber":"","submissionId":20190000277,"ear":"NO","id":"268af69c34d34f41a63d388e58836840","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-08-12T18:53:03.5570000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["ARC-E-DAA-TN36851","Report Number: ARC-E-DAA-TN36851"],"fundingNumbers":[{"number":"NNA14AB82C","submissionId":20190000277,"id":"1e0a749a41644fc38e6270de18c59975","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"},{"number":"NNA13AC87C","submissionId":20190000277,"id":"c52e1f3691344219bfe5015e28b44509","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"},{"number":"NNA14AA60C","submissionId":20190000277,"id":"e5024a2892c84310b2d479b456bf9eda","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"},{"number":"NNA16BD14C","submissionId":20190000277,"id":"d9f8f4f4b93a40fe8b099e43b67b9430","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"}],"title":"Biosensor Integration Development ExMC/Canadian Space Agency Collaboration","stiType":"ABSTRACT","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2019-01-31T11:51:05.2300000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissi