0170009788,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Lindsey, A."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"76917163a134455f85161c3d44148136"},{"sequence":3,"submissionId":20170009788,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Marker, N."},"organization":{"name":"SGT, Inc.","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"552ed26523244dbf8891efc69064c55f"},{"sequence":4,"submissionId":20170009788,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Wolfe, S."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"9911771ca3e1493287a54a21b127cb30"},{"sequence":5,"submissionId":20170009788,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Winther, S."},"organization":{"name":"Wyle Labs., Inc.","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"3068a923b3b0474c9156551f5fcd9582"},{"sequence":6,"submissionId":20170009788,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Ronzano, K."},"organization":{"name":"Wyle Labs., Inc.","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"8ce9c6300bda4cd5b7c31fa3dbecce8d"},{"sequence":7,"submissionId":20170009788,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Bolles, D."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"e90e5bfce1284dfb9a7d7686467e070c"},{"sequence":8,"submissionId":20170009788,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Toscano, W."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"68e910b6274a4bf485c93ed447f758eb"},{"sequence":9,"submissionId":20170009788,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Shaw, T."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","location":"Moffett Field, CA, United States"}},"id":"e6029d44710049be9fa803b9e93582a0"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Presentation","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20170009788,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2017-10-11T14:06:00.7470000+00:00","center":{"code":"ARC","name":"Ames Research Center","id":"4540cd94d24c4bf29f8773a27faf96b2"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"Mission constraints will challenge the delivery of medical care on a long-term, deep space explorationmission. This type of mission will be restricted in the availability of medical knowledge, skills, procedures and resourcesto prevent, diagnose, and treat in-flight medical events. Challenges to providing medical care are anticipated, includingresource and resupply constraints, delayed communications and no ability for medical evacuation. The Medical DataArchitecture (MDA) project will enable medical care capability in this constrained environment.The first version of thesystem, called Test Bed 1, includes capabilities for automated data collection, data storage and data retrieval to provideinformation to the Crew Medical Officer (CMO). Test Bed 1 seeks to establish a data architecture foundation and developa scalable data management system through modular design and standardized interfaces. In addition, it will demonstrateto stakeholders the potential for an improved, automated, flow of data to and from the medical system over the currentmethods employed on the International Space Station (ISS). It integrates a set of external devices, software andprocesses, and a Subjective, Objective, Assessment, and Plan (SOAP) note commonly used by clinicians. Medical datalike electrocardiogram plots, heart rate, skin temperature, respiration rate, medications taken, and more are collectedfrom devices and stored in the Electronic Medical Records (EMR) system, and reported to crew and clinician. Devicesintegrated include the Astroskin biosensor vest and IMED CARDIAX electrocardiogram (ECG) device with INEED MDECG Glove, and the NASA-developed Medical Dose Tracker application.The system is designed to be operated as astandalone system, and can be deployed in a variety of environments, from a laptop to a data center. The system isprimarily composed of open-source software tools, and is designed to be modular, so new capabilities can be added. Thesoftware components and integration methods will be discussed.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","meetings":[{"country":"United States","submissionId":20170009788,"endDate":"2017-01-26T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"organizationId":"0bba4b66c88d4f6b9af09a68495f6606","meta":{"organization":{"name":"NASA Headquarters","location":"Washington, DC, United States"}},"meetingId":"b24eb7bb33f2456fa8214506b1972198","id":"0cc43f2804e046a49f122889d486e151"}],"name":"NASA Human Research Program Investigators'' Workshop (HRP IWS 2017)","location":"Galveston, TX","id":"b24eb7bb33f2456fa8214506b1972198","startDate":"2017-01-23T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20170009788,"id":"793032305cd746d6a2fdc1bb41365afc","publicationDate":"2017-01-24T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20170009788.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20170009788/downloads/20170009788.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20170009788/downloads/20170009788.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20170009788/downloads/20170009788.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"}],"aggregations":{"created":{"buckets":[{"key_as_string":"2019","key":1546300800000,"doc_count":3},{"key_as_string":"2017","key":1483228800000,"doc_count":2},{"key_as_string":"2015","key":1420070400000,"doc_count":1},{"key_as_string":"2018","key":1514764800000,"doc_count":1}]},"author":{"doc_count_error_upper_bound":0,"sum_other_doc_count":3,"buckets":[{"key":"Krihak, M.","doc_count":5},{"key":"Shaw, T.","doc_count":5},{"key":"Toscano, W.","doc_count":5},{"key":"Lindsey, A.","doc_count":4},{"key":"Marker, N.","doc_count":4},{"key":"Middour, C.","doc_count":4},{"key":"Winther, S.","doc_count":4},{"key":"Wolfe, S.","doc_count":4},{"key":"Bolles, D.","doc_count":2},{"key":"Ronz